<title>CANADA: TransCanada PipeLines CEO sees higher EPS.</title>
<headline>TransCanada PipeLines CEO sees higher EPS.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>TransCanada PipeLines Ltd Chief Executive Officer George Watson said on Thursday he &quot;can't argue&quot; with analysts' estimates for earnings per share in 1997 of C$1.90 to C$1.95.</p>
<p>At TransCanada's annual meeting, Watson also said the company set a target to produce earnings of C$3.0 per share in the year 2002.</p>
<p>TransCanada posted earnings per share in 1996 of C$1.85.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100))</p>
</text>
